.TH DMESG 8 "August 2, 2026"
.SH NAME
dmesg \- display the kernel message buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dmesg
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dmesg
displays the messages retained by the kernel since the current boot.
The messages are returned as a non-destructive snapshot of the common
kernel message ring, so running
.B dmesg
does not clear it or interfere with another reader.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B kern.msgbuf
Read-only sysctl node containing the retained messages in chronological order.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sysctl (8)
